{"h":3390,"w":2400,"lines":[{"c":1,"y":0.04941860483360061,"h":0.014593194719612845,"t":"Test 4","x":0.090349074655841591,"w":0.06160164515177409},{"w":0.31006159464518224,"x":0.090349079372147784,"c":1,"y":0.097345132489844111,"h":0.01457347194705394,"t":"READING PASSAGE 2"},{"y":0.13362831910501527,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading","x":0.090349063962999021,"w":0.82546203613281255,"h":0.018987959465094462,"c":1},{"h":0.017826361079483322,"w":0.11100238800048827,"c":1,"x":0.090289360307468439,"t":"Passage 2.","y":0.15097054009137367},{"w":0.24907488505045572,"y":0.18719304821655702,"x":0.38575507358896599,"h":0.025152632901802252,"c":1,"t":"Deep-sea mining"},{"y":0.22779869720465629,"c":1,"x":0.10671579885902721,"t":"Bacteria from the ocean floor can beat superbugs and cancer. But habitats are at risk","w":0.80300654093424484,"h":0.019194530385785336},{"x":0.33470225687421018,"w":0.34496920267740883,"t":"from the hunger for marine minerals","y":0.24709302327656646,"h":0.017508746459420799,"c":1},{"t":"A When Professor Mat Upton found that a microbe from a deep-sea sponge was killing","x":0.088295698954880111,"y":0.28052325583765225,"w":0.75154001871744791,"h":0.017441860412777732,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"pathogenic bugs in his laboratory, he realised it could be a breakthrough in the fight against","x":0.1354688633903682,"y":0.29789160279374072,"w":0.75370890299479165,"h":0.019016407654348755},{"h":0.020107382940331764,"x":0.13545419885846588,"y":0.31486402356853316,"c":1,"w":0.77016774495442708,"t":"antibiotic-resistant superbugs, which are responsible for thousands of deaths a year in the UK"},{"t":"alone. Further tests confirmed that an antibiotic from the sponge bacteria, found living more","h":0.020885612690343169,"c":1,"x":0.13545533736354487,"y":0.33128696007836367,"w":0.75989613850911453},{"t":"than 700 metres under the sea at the Rockall trough in the north-east Atlantic, was previously","w":0.76796712239583331,"x":0.13552362569177073,"y":0.35162241901693103,"h":0.017699115044247704,"c":1},{"w":0.74537989298502605,"t":"unknown to science, boosting its potential as a life-saving medicine. But Upton, and other","x":0.13552360579516196,"c":1,"h":0.016224188790560423,"y":0.37050147502792552},{"h":0.01604839820074111,"t":"scientists who view the deep ocean and its wealth of unique and undocumented species as a","c":1,"y":0.38808139546402032,"w":0.75564682006835926,"x":0.1355236124371722},{"t":"prospecting ground for new medicines, fear such potential will be lost in the rush to exploit the","c":1,"w":0.78234085083007809,"x":0.13552361968714802,"y":0.40552325592634997,"h":0.016010667581473959},{"t":"deep sea's equally rich metal and mineral resources.","h":0.017447863215893644,"c":1,"x":0.13552361775923363,"w":0.43326487223307297,"y":0.42296511608721588},{"y":0.45772905434347044,"t":"'We're looking at the bioactive potential of marine resources, to see if there are any more","c":1,"w":0.76604502360026039,"h":0.019640204055471067,"x":0.13339593279943718},{"w":0.71663243611653638,"y":0.47669616533293757,"x":0.13552361756737136,"t":"medicines or drugs down there before we destroy it for ever;' says Upton, a medical","c":1,"h":0.017489881149787223},{"w":0.77412729899088528,"h":0.017527611769054485,"x":0.13552361938364896,"t":"microbiologist at the University of Plymouth. He is among many scientists urging a halt to","y":0.49410029517882048,"c":1},{"t":"deep-sea mining, asking for time to weigh up the pros and cons. 'In sustainability terms,","c":1,"y":0.51150442500556692,"x":0.13552361298430091,"w":0.75564682006835937,"h":0.017699115044247815},{"h":0.017537901886796492,"x":0.1355236066965628,"w":0.77002054850260404,"c":1,"y":0.52906976746063916,"t":"this could be a better way of exploiting the economic potential of the deep sea,' he argues."},{"x":0.13552361941618585,"t":"Oceanographers using remotely operated vehicles have spotted many new species. Among","w":0.77412729899088539,"h":0.016046683274890783,"c":1,"y":0.54796511639388179},{"c":1,"w":0.72689936319986981,"t":"them have been sea cucumbers with tails allowing them to sail along the ocean floor,","y":0.56686046523149491,"h":0.016030390354032642,"x":0.13552362425418304},{"h":0.023071588386828212,"c":1,"x":0.13538312520941229,"t":"and a rare 'Dumbo' octopus, found 3,000 metres under the Pacific Ocean, off the coast","y":0.58038205290610201,"w":0.74154581705729161},{"x":0.13552362503724719,"w":0.75154001871744791,"t":"of California. Any one of these could offer lifesaving potential. Upton estimates it could","y":0.6017441861620404,"h":0.015988371857499684,"c":1},{"y":0.61917404101997264,"x":0.135523612704568,"h":0.01600037746373173,"c":1,"t":"take up to a decade for a newly discovered antibiotic to become a medicine - but the race","w":0.76386037190755207},{"w":0.57084187825520827,"c":1,"t":"towards commercial mining in the ocean abyss has already begun.","y":0.63805309749865757,"x":0.13347023120138629,"h":0.016016669821950158},{"t":"C","x":0.088295687575091319,"w":0.018480493227640782,"y":0.67296511648657797,"h":0.013081394746943587,"c":1},{"t":"The deep sea contains more nickel, cobalt and rare earth metals than all land reserves","x":0.12525667094426696,"y":0.67286135672043934,"h":0.014749262536873253,"w":0.72279261271158857,"c":1},{"y":0.69026548647459574,"w":0.74127309163411459,"h":0.016224188790560423,"c":1,"t":"combined, according to the US Geological Survey. Mining corporations argue that deep-","x":0.13552361835132046},{"y":0.70784883729949799,"h":0.016044967786400743,"c":1,"t":"sea exploration could help diversify the supply of metals and point to the fact that demand","x":0.13552362524440564,"w":0.75154001871744791},{"x":0.13552361269621685,"w":0.76386037190755218,"y":0.72674418616179071,"t":"for resources such as copper, aluminium, cobalt for electric car batteries and other metals to","c":1,"h":0.016028675428182315},{"t":"power technology and smartphones, is soaring. They say that deep-sea mining could yield","c":1,"w":0.75154001871744791,"x":0.1355236250672876,"y":0.74418604662651411,"h":0.015990944246275229},{"t":"far superior ore to land mining with little, if any, waste. Different methods of extraction exist,","y":0.76017441862820945,"c":1,"x":0.13552361324171747,"h":0.017441860412777621,"w":0.78028747558593747},{"w":0.77823410034179685,"h":0.017455580944860216,"c":1,"t":"but most involve employing some form of converted machinery previously used in terrestrial","y":0.77905604693099206,"x":0.13552360673653577},{"y":0.79646017712641259,"c":1,"w":0.78028747558593747,"t":"mining to excavate materials from the sea floor, at depths of up to 6,000 metres, then drawing","h":0.017493311001487877,"x":0.13552362231996729},{"y":0.81533923278495291,"t":"a seawater slurry, containing rock and other solid particles, from the sea floor to ships on","w":0.73921971638997386,"h":0.016056115929707682,"x":0.13552361197186619,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"the surface. The slurry is then 'de-watered' and transferred to another vessel for shipping.","x":0.13552363081251873,"w":0.74537984212239594,"h":0.017699115044247704,"y":0.83126843681811047},{"h":0.019456025070145322,"c":1,"t":"Extracted seawater is pumped back down and discharged close to the sea floor:","x":0.13546061067591608,"w":0.66130406697591149,"y":0.8496980068275517},{"h":0.011627907316944963,"t":"88","y":0.92441860443261281,"w":0.026694043477376292,"c":1,"x":0.088295688639477482},{"t":"IELTSXpress.com","w":0.45294118245442705,"c":1,"y":0.94166666659226195,"x":0.51176470218665204,"h":0.04166666666666663}]}